  "route": {
    "route_id": "syria-trunk",
    "name": "Damascus-Aleppo Railway (Syrian trunk)",
    "name_arabic": "سكة حديد دمشق-حلب",
    "countries": "Syria",
    "gauge_mm": 1435,
    "year_opened": 1906,
    "era": "historic",
    "color": "#b45309",
    "corridor_confidence": "high",
    "description": "Syrian standard-gauge north-south trunk; the connector to Aleppo",
    "notes": "The internal Syrian standard-gauge trunk; the physical link from the Levant routes to the Baghdad Railway.  [established] The Homs-Hama-Aleppo section is the DHP standard-gauge northern line (opened 1902-1906); the DIRECT Damascus-Homs standard-gauge link (194 km) opened only in 1983 (before that Damascus connected north via Rayak / the narrow gauge). So the full through trunk dates variously 1906-1983.  [connections] This is the missing SPINE that ties the network together: it meets the Beirut-Damascus and Hejaz lines at Damascus; the Rayak-Baalbek and Tripoli-Homs lines at Homs; the Syrian coastal and Euphrates lines; and the Baghdad Railway at Aleppo (-> Turkey and Iraq). GSGS 2061/9 (1916): trunk drawn as COMPLETED railway. Note: the 1916 map routes Damascus↔Homs via Rayak/Baalbek (the direct An-Nabk alignment we model postdates 1916) — An-Nabk not shown on the 1916 trunk; Maarat al-Numan drawn as a town, not a station on the line.",
    "history": "The standard-gauge (1,435 mm) spine of the Syrian network. Its northern half (Homs-Hama-Aleppo) is the French DHP 'prolongements' opened 1902-1906; the Damascus-Homs section was completed as standard gauge in 1983, giving a continuous Damascus-Aleppo trunk.",
    "verification_status": "unverified",
